<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#PartSpecShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#RequiredPartsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Required Parts. A required part role declared by the conformed profile is missing."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#RequiredPartsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of abnd:Asset Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#RequiredPartsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Required Parts Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#RequiredPartsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Namespace prefix declarations reused by SHACL SPARQL constraints and rules. This is validation infrastructure, not a property of parsed data."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Used by named SHACL SPARQL constraints/rules in this module. Not intended for instance-data assertions."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "prefixes"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#boundBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The binding convention used to associate a member with its asset, selected from the declared BindingKind individuals."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#boundBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#carriesAspect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The aspect ontology whose properties this part contributes. Drives facet lifting. An annotation-style link, NOT an owl:import — orthogonality is preserved."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#carriesAspect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#describedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The BDDO byte-layout struct describing this part's bytes (optional). The struct's local name also NAMES the part for cross-part references: HEL's `asset` root resolves `asset.<StructLocalName>.<field>` through this property, so a sidecar described by a struct named Header is reached as asset.Header. Two PartSpecs of one BundleProfile therefore MUST NOT be describedBy structs sharing a local name."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#describedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#extension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Filename extension identifying this member (e.g. \".dbf\"). MULTIPLE values are alternatives, not a requirement for several files: the part is whichever ONE of them is present. Some formats name a single member by its content rather than a fixed suffix -- an ESRI .hdr labelled raster carries its grid in .bil, .bip or .bsq according to the LAYOUT keyword, and .flt when floating point -- so one PartSpec with several extensions describes one part, not three. A profile that genuinely expects several files declares several PartSpecs."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#extension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#hasPart> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A member resource belonging to a compound asset; the relation represents logical membership, not a byte offset."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#hasPart> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#maxParts> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Most files that may match this spec. Absent means unbounded -- the normal case for a pattern like \"measurement/*.tiff\", where the count is a property of the data rather than of the format."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#maxParts> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#minParts> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Fewest files that must match this spec. Defaults to 1 when abnd:required is true and 0 otherwise, so the boolean remains sufficient for a single-file member; declare a count only when a spec matches MANY files, which a pattern makes possible and an extension never did."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#minParts> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#nestedProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "For a member that is itself a structured directory: the BundleProfile its contents conform to, rooted at that member. Lets a profile compose rather than flatten -- a SAFE product describes its annotation directory once instead of enumerating every file in it."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#nestedProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#partIndex> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ordinal of a Part within a segmented/concatenated Asset."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#partIndex> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#partOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The asset of which a part is a logical member."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#partOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#partRole> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The role a Part or PartSpec plays, from a part-role register bound by the profile."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#partRole> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#partSpec> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A part specification declared by a bundle profile, describing a role and its structural or discovery expectations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#partSpec> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#pathPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A glob matching this member's path relative to the asset root, e.g. \"measurement/*.tiff\". `*` matches within one path segment, `**` across segments, `?` one character. As with abnd:extension, MULTIPLE values are ALTERNATIVES. Mutually exclusive with abnd:extension, which is the flat-sibling shorthand for the pattern \"*<ext>\"."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#pathPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#primary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Marks the PartSpec whose instance is the Asset's primaryPart."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#primary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#primaryPart> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The recognition anchor / manifest part (e.g. .shp, .gltf, .mpd)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#primaryPart> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#required> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Whether the part described by a part specification is required by the bundle contract."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#required> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#stem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Shared basename of a naming-convention bundle (e.g. \"roads\")."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#stem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for compound assets, their members and reusable membership profiles. Discovery/binding, semantic membership and physical byte location are separate concerns. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
